# Code Quality

## Style

- Prefer simple, robust JavaScript — no build step for runtime code
- async/await for asynchronous operations
- JSDoc on public methods where helpful
- Use `this.log.*` in adapter code — never `console.log` in production adapter code
- Prototype script may use `log()` (javascript adapter API)
- Tabs, double quotes (match inventwo `prettier.config.mjs` when scaffold exists)
- ESLint via `@iobroker/eslint-config` — run `npm run lint` after every change

## Resource cleanup

Clear timers and close WebSockets in `onUnload()`; always call `callback()`:

```javascript
onUnload(callback) {
	try {
		if (this.pollTimer) {
			this.clearInterval(this.pollTimer);
			this.pollTimer = null;
		}
		if (this.crealityWs) {
			this.crealityWs.close();
			this.crealityWs = null;
		}
		callback();
	} catch (error) {
		this.log.error(`Error during unload: ${error.message}`);
		callback();
	}
}
```

## Error handling

- Wrap async/API work in try/catch; log errors, do not crash the adapter
- Network failures: set `info.connection` / `online` false; wait for next poll
- Do not retry failed HTTP/WS calls in a tight loop
- **Printer powered off** (`EHOSTUNREACH`, `ECONNREFUSED`, `Timeout`, …): log **once** at **info**, not warn; log **once** at info when reachable again. Do not flood the log every poll cycle.

## HTTP / WS

- **Preferred:** native `node:http` / `node:https`
- **Avoid:** axios, request
- Creality control API: WebSocket `ws://host:9999/` JSON `{ "method": "set", "params": { … } }`
- Moonraker: HTTP `http://host:7125/…` (and G-code via `/printer/gcode/script`)

## Dependencies

- Node.js >= 22
- `@iobroker/adapter-core`; avoid unnecessary dependencies
- Prefer built-in Node modules (`WebSocket` on Node 22+)
